   "section": "rules",
   "tr": {}
  },
  {
   "en": "The causative is the sentence for work you <strong>arrange</strong> rather than do. You are still the subject — it is your money and your decision — but the hands belong to somebody you usually do not bother to name.",
   "kind": "chrome",
   "where": "[When to use it] div.trail-wrap > div.camp#rules > p.chart-note",
   "section": "rules",
   "tr": {}
  },
  {
